<body>
    <%- include("partials/navbar", { activePage }) %>

    <main class="page-container narrow-container">
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <a href="forum-main">Forum</a> / <a href="forum-main#english-books">English Books</a>
        </nav>

        <article class="discussion-card">
            <span class="tag">English Books</span>
            <h1>Which translation of The Little Prince should I read?</h1>
            <p class="post-meta">Posted by <strong>Linh Nguyen</strong> on 18 July 2026</p>
            <p>I want to read <em>The Little Prince</em> in English for the first time. I found translations by
                Katherine Woods and Richard Howard. Which version is easier for an intermediate English learner?</p>
            <div class="post-actions">
                <button type="button">Edit topic</button>
                <button type="button">Delete topic</button>
            </div>
        </article>

        <section aria-labelledby="reply-heading">
            <h2 id="reply-heading" class="section-title">4 replies</h2>
            <div class="reply-list">
                <article class="reply-card">
                    <header class="reply-header">
                        <strong>Alex Pham</strong>
                        <span>18 July 2026, 10:15</span>
                    </header>
                    <p>Richard Howard's translation uses more modern English. I found it clearer when I first read the
                        story.</p>
                    <a class="reply-link" href="#reply-form">Reply</a>
                </article>

                <article class="reply-card nested-reply">
                    <header class="reply-header">
                        <strong>Linh Nguyen</strong>
                        <span>18 July 2026, 11:02</span>
                    </header>
                    <p><strong>Replying to Alex:</strong> Thank you. Modern wording sounds better for my first reading.</p>
                    <a class="reply-link" href="#reply-form">Reply</a>
                </article>

                <article class="reply-card">
                    <header class="reply-header">
                        <strong>Mai Hoang</strong>
                        <span>18 July 2026, 14:40</span>
                    </header>
                    <p>Katherine Woods has a more classic style. You could read one chapter from each version before
                        choosing.</p>
                    <a class="reply-link" href="#reply-form">Reply</a>
                </article>

                <article class="reply-card">
                    <header class="reply-header">
                        <strong>Daniel Lee</strong>
                        <span>19 July 2026, 09:20</span>
                    </header>
                    <p>I also recommend Richard Howard for a learner. The sentences feel direct, but the meaning is
                        still beautiful.</p>
                    <a class="reply-link" href="#reply-form">Reply</a>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="reply-form-section" aria-labelledby="reply-form-heading">
            <h2 id="reply-form-heading">Add your reply</h2>
            <form id="reply-form" action="forum-topic" method="get">
                <label for="reply-message">Your message</label>
                <textarea id="reply-message" name="message" rows="6" placeholder="Share a helpful answer..."
                    required></textarea>
                <button class="button" type="submit">Post reply</button>
            </form>
        </section>
    </main>

    <%- include("partials/footer") %>

